{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-166",
  "title": "Concepts (v2)",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Concepts (v2)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "*presence in absence. the seen and unseen.*"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**type:** serif with breath. something like portrait or lyon. ghostly but firm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**color scheme:** bone white, deep ash, old photo sepia, with sudden punctures of gold or crimson."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**photo treatment:** archival blur. layered textures. soft vignettes. photos feel like memory—faded, but stubborn."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-7",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**overall narrative & themes:** explores how black lives in france are erased from national narratives but remain embedded in the culture. themes of surveillance, erasure, and haunting presence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**iconography/illustration:** thin line sketches. colonial-era maps glitched. silhouettes. monuments cracked open."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-9",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**animation treatment:** slow reveals. ghosting effects. text fades in like a whisper. hover interactions bring clarity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**logomark:** fragmented \"F\" for france. part of it missing, part reclaimed. or an eye, half-closed, half-seeing."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "*to live. loudly. black joy as resistance.*"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-22",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-15",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**type:** bold grotesque sans. think neue haas grotesk or something playful like ohno grotesk."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-16",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**color scheme:** ultramarine, ochre, blood orange, warm browns. electric joy with grounded roots."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-17",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**photo treatment:** high contrast. sharp color overlays. candid black life—movement, smiles, protests, dance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-18",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**overall narrative & themes:** centers the vitality of black french life. joy, community, rhythm, presence. flips the narrative from marginalization to celebration."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-19",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**iconography/illustration:** afro combs, metro signs, soundwaves, ancestral patterns, carnival masks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-20",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**animation treatment:** bounce. parallax. rhythm in transitions. hover states that feel like music."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-21",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**logomark:** a single spiral—growth, movement, history never linear."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "*what’s left behind. and what we carry forward.*"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-33",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-26",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**type:** monospace or hybrid serif-sans. archival meets modern."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-27",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**color scheme:** parchment beige, carbon black, slate gray, dusk blue. introspective tones."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-28",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**photo treatment:** mixed media collage—old documents layered with contemporary portraits. ephemera scanned and recontextualized."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-29",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**overall narrative & themes:** deals with memory, legacy, archives, and resistance through history. how black french life has always been there, just not always recorded."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-30",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**iconography/illustration:** fingerprints, ink stains, paper edges, typewriter marks, census docs, protest signs."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-31",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**animation treatment:** typewriter effect, scroll-triggered reveals, glitch transitions. time folding in on itself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-32",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**logomark:** a fingerprint turning into a map. identity as geography."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}